(4412922, 635808, 25890, '<td valign="top">It appears that this location has a lot of potential. I''m not sure you found the best composition there, though. I, for example, would be tempted to walk into the water, closer to the rocks on the left, and shoot from a low angle to emphasize the shape and form of the wreck as well as those nice, juicy colors and texture on it. I keep a pair of wellington boots in the trunk of my car just for opportunities like this. Exposure needs reworking too; I don''t like blown-out highlights, especially in this type of photographs. In addition, the bottom part, even though there''s still some barely visible detail, is too dark, in my opinion.</td>', 'It appears that this location has a lot of potential. I''m not sure you found the best composition there, though. I, for example, would be tempted to walk into the water, closer to the rocks on the left, and shoot from a low angle to emphasize the shape and form of the wreck as well as those nice, juicy colors and texture on it. I keep a pair of wellington boots in the trunk of my car just for opportunities like this. Exposure needs reworking too; I don''t like blown-out highlights, especially in this type of photographs. In addition, the bottom part, even though there''s still some barely visible detail, is too dark, in my opinion.', '2008-01-22 05:36:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4412925, 635622, 34938, '<td valign="top">oh wow!<br/>LOVE the duotone/sepia for this as it reminds me of some olf African Safari images from 100 years ago<br/>Love the drama in the shot<br/>Did you use IR for this?<br/>Love the light and shade, you really made the most of this image in the edit...<br/>I was going to guess this as a lesley <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=16241" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Goodman</a> image, but not sure...<br/> <br/>8 from me</td>', 'oh wow!LOVE the duotone/sepia for this as it reminds me of some olf African Safari images from 100 years agoLove the drama in the shotDid you use IR for this?Love the light and shade, you really made the most of this image in the edit...I was going to guess this as a lesley  Goodman image, but not sure... 8 from me', '2008-01-22 05:38:17.000000', NULL, 1),
