(4429806, 633717, 52500, '<td valign="top">Well, crap.  Now this is the second image I have seen that could be MAK''s.  Even though these guys are the same subject in a similar place as MAK''s ribbon winner, I''m gonna guess the other one''s his and this isn''t.  The sky doesn''t seem right, and the other one is super MAK style.  Oh yeah, very nice pic regardless!  (it''s just fun to guess)</td>', 'Well, crap.  Now this is the second image I have seen that could be MAK''s.  Even though these guys are the same subject in a similar place as MAK''s ribbon winner, I''m gonna guess the other one''s his and this isn''t.  The sky doesn''t seem right, and the other one is super MAK style.  Oh yeah, very nice pic regardless!  (it''s just fun to guess)', '2008-01-27 18:30:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4429807, 636005, 52500, '<td valign="top">I don''t know what the hell is going on here, but this is damn cool looking!</td>', 'I don''t know what the hell is going on here, but this is damn cool looking!', '2008-01-27 18:31:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4429809, 635473, 36999, '<td valign="top">when shooting horses and other large animals use a longer focal length to keep the distortion from being so bad on the animal.<br/>this is a nice composition but the horse is so deformed by the short lens it hurts this image a lot.  there is a place for shorty lenses on horses but not when the horse is part of a landscape.  Gorgeous place to shoot!  and lovely image otherwise.</td>', 'when shooting horses and other large animals use a longer focal length to keep the distortion from being so bad on the animal.this is a nice composition but the horse is so deformed by the short lens it hurts this image a lot.  there is a place for shorty lenses on horses but not when the horse is part of a landscape.  Gorgeous place to shoot!  and lovely image otherwise.', '2008-01-27 18:32:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4429816, 636041, 36999, '<td valign="top">nice to see it in sunrise instead of sunset.</td>', 'nice to see it in sunrise instead of sunset.', '2008-01-27 18:35:09.000000', NULL, 1),
