(4433100, 632900, 85886, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8 for what it''s worth.  I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=42013" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mpeters</a> - technically this shot is spot on.  To mark it below a 5 is harsh.  Lighten up DPC!</td>', 'I gave this an 8 for what it''s worth.  I agree with  mpeters - technically this shot is spot on.  To mark it below a 5 is harsh.  Lighten up DPC!', '2008-01-28 13:46:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4433129, 634695, 67237, '<td valign="top">Vey interesting image for a large print. But this kind of subject suffers too much at dpc resolution. Just a very few dpchallengers have the secret (in a safelock probably) on how to process this kind of image in order to preserve a fair amount of detail while eliminating noise color artifacts. I am not one of them though.<br/> <br/>It looks like the NR filter has reduced the amount of detail a bit too much. I think a tighter crop at the top would have helped in the overall balance, but the main problem here is the limitation of dpc resolutuion.<br/> <br/>Exposure is very good, I like how the unavoidable blown out lights are not pure whites. Exposure of the crowds under shadow looks abot 1/3 f stop too low, or maybe there were just not any people up there?. :-) <br/> <br/>You are getting better and better all the time!!</td>', 'Vey interesting image for a large print. But this kind of subject suffers too much at dpc resolution. Just a very few dpchallengers have the secret (in a safelock probably) on how to process this kind of image in order to preserve a fair amount of detail while eliminating noise color artifacts. I am not one of them though. It looks like the NR filter has reduced the amount of detail a bit too much. I think a tighter crop at the top would have helped in the overall balance, but the main problem here is the limitation of dpc resolutuion. Exposure is very good, I like how the unavoidable blown out lights are not pure whites. Exposure of the crowds under shadow looks abot 1/3 f stop too low, or maybe there were just not any people up there?. :-)  You are getting better and better all the time!!', '2008-01-28 13:53:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4433130, 634232, 67723, '<td valign="top">Hey man, congrats on a nice shot.  can''t believe I beat you!</td>', 'Hey man, congrats on a nice shot.  can''t believe I beat you!', '2008-01-28 13:53:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4433138, 634509, 61961, '<td valign="top">Hi, Haneck.  This was also one of my 10s, and I do think it was way underrated.  Sometimes I don''t connect with a photo if the animal is facing away from the camera, but in this location it makes perfect sense and complements the half-silhouette of the other horse.  Plus you''ve got the lovely tail contrasting so nicely with the darker browns and blacks.  Good textures, tones -- don''t let the relatively low placement determine how you feel about this photo.</td>', 'Hi, Haneck.  This was also one of my 10s, and I do think it was way underrated.  Sometimes I don''t connect with a photo if the animal is facing away from the camera, but in this location it makes perfect sense and complements the half-silhouette of the other horse.  Plus you''ve got the lovely tail contrasting so nicely with the darker browns and blacks.  Good textures, tones -- don''t let the relatively low placement determine how you feel about this photo.', '2008-01-28 13:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
