(4439848, 633442, 67855, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bennettjamie:</b></div><hr/><i> THis is beautiful. Do you mind sharing how you get this look to your photographs. Almost unreal look? I love it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi Jamie (i see your personnal portfolio, you are so pretty !)<br/>To make long time exposure at broad daylight, you need a tripod &amp; a neutral grey filter (Hoya ND400 now B+W ND 1000)<br/>Thanks ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by bennettjamie: THis is beautiful. Do you mind sharing how you get this look to your photographs. Almost unreal look? I love it!  Hi Jamie (i see your personnal portfolio, you are so pretty !)To make long time exposure at broad daylight, you need a tripod & a neutral grey filter (Hoya ND400 now B+W ND 1000)Thanks ;)', '2008-01-30 12:10:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4439852, 633442, 67855, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LanndonKane:</b></div><hr/><i> I just keep coming back to this!! Any chance of posting the original, and maybe some post processing steps for the rest of us learners? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hello LanndonKane,<br/>hum...for processing :<br/>Colors balance correction, levels, sharpen...<br/>Thanks</td>', 'Originally posted by LanndonKane: I just keep coming back to this!! Any chance of posting the original, and maybe some post processing steps for the rest of us learners?  Hello LanndonKane,hum...for processing :Colors balance correction, levels, sharpen...Thanks', '2008-01-30 12:12:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4439929, 633442, 67855, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Aurel78:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bennettjamie:</b></div><hr/><i> THis is beautiful. Do you mind sharing how you get this look to your photographs. Almost unreal look? I love it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi Jamie (i see your personnal portfolio, you are so pretty !)<br/>To make long time exposure at broad daylight, you need a tripod &amp; a neutral grey filter (Hoya ND400 now B+W ND 1000)<br/>Thanks ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>AND...<br/>* LOW ISO (50-200) because the long time exposure is sensitive to a noise !<br/>* Lock the mirror (for reduce vibrations)<br/>:)</td>', 'Originally posted by Aurel78: Originally posted by bennettjamie: THis is beautiful. Do you mind sharing how you get this look to your photographs. Almost unreal look? I love it!  Hi Jamie (i see your personnal portfolio, you are so pretty !)To make long time exposure at broad daylight, you need a tripod & a neutral grey filter (Hoya ND400 now B+W ND 1000)Thanks ;)  AND...* LOW ISO (50-200) because the long time exposure is sensitive to a noise !* Lock the mirror (for reduce vibrations):)', '2008-01-30 12:34:27.000000', NULL, 0),
