(4446256, 632958, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is so beautiful!  What a gorgeous expression of Tokyo.   I''m happy it did so well in the challenge.   6.3+ in a Best of 2007 photo is quite an accomplishment!   <br/> <br/></td>', 'This is so beautiful!  What a gorgeous expression of Tokyo.   I''m happy it did so well in the challenge.   6.3+ in a Best of 2007 photo is quite an accomplishment!    ', '2008-02-01 10:33:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4446385, 634385, 61651, '<td valign="top">Wow, if this were mine, it would certainly be the best of my year.  Great work, this is so very evocative.  So many stories to be got from this.</td>', 'Wow, if this were mine, it would certainly be the best of my year.  Great work, this is so very evocative.  So many stories to be got from this.', '2008-02-01 11:09:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4446389, 633703, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Stunning land/seascape.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, it is very well balanced.  The shore "leads" to the city in the background, but is broken up by the rocks in the almost center.  This is very effective in adding interest to the shot.  Also, I think it works well that there is a lot of foreground to the shot.  <br/> <br/>Technically, the exposure, focus, etc. work well together to make a great shot.  I think the long exposure worked particularly well to give that misty ghosty feeling to the water.  The lights in the background give just enough color contrast to work well, and give some "life" to the shot.<br/> <br/>Overall, I think you have a great shot, and did fairly well in a competition with a lot of awesome shots.<br/> <br/>Good work.<br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Stunning land/seascape. Compositionally, it is very well balanced.  The shore "leads" to the city in the background, but is broken up by the rocks in the almost center.  This is very effective in adding interest to the shot.  Also, I think it works well that there is a lot of foreground to the shot.   Technically, the exposure, focus, etc. work well together to make a great shot.  I think the long exposure worked particularly well to give that misty ghosty feeling to the water.  The lights in the background give just enough color contrast to work well, and give some "life" to the shot. Overall, I think you have a great shot, and did fairly well in a competition with a lot of awesome shots. Good work.Karma', '2008-02-01 11:10:34.000000', NULL, 0),
